In article <1992Oct30.184215.4994@zip.eecs.umich.edu>, katkere@eecs.umich.edu (Arun L. Katkere) writes:

|> Another question about the same game. I sometimes kill shk's by
|> collecting a lot of projectiles and throwing them from outside the shop
|> until I get a lot of hits, and then finshing him off with a good
|> weapon. Usually the shk gets angry and stays angry after the first
|> hit. But this shk, (Gaziantep, who charged me 18406995 zorkmids) gets
|> angry on the first hit, but is peaceful by the time I enter the shop.
|> How's that? Is this related in any way to the exhorbitant charge?
I (think I) found the answer to this. If the shopkeeper has never seen
you, (s)he will no longer be angry when you enter the shop. (S)He will
never see you if you are invisible. So, if you a lot of projectiles,
and if you are invisible you can keep throwing weapons at the shk
until (s)he is killed. (S)He will never be angry with you even if
can't kill him/her.
